The outer expression keeps this classification relevant only to variants that
contain the robotic fastening resource.

## 4.3 Control-data connection classification by voltage

### Purpose

Classify the existing **Control-data connection** with the selected operating
voltage while retaining its production-data meaning.

This example demonstrates typed feature-value conditions using the existing
enumeration feature `feature-operating-voltage`.

### Create it through the interface

1. In the Variation Points graph, find **Control-data connection**.
2. Double-click its displayed **Tags** attribute.
3. Enter the following definition.

| Field | Enter or select |
|---|---|
| Name | Control-data connection voltage classification |
| Kind | `primitiveTag` (prefilled) |
| Target type | `element` (prefilled) |
| Target | Control-data connection (prefilled) |
| Feature expression | `feature-data-recording OR feature-advanced-analytics` |
| Typed feature-value conditions | Leave blank |
| Property path | `tags` (prefilled) |
| Realization domain | `structure` |

4. Create both value rules. The feature expression is blank in each rule
   because the distinction is made by the typed condition.

| Order | Rule feature expression | Typed conditions | Realized value |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 1 | Leave blank | `feature-operating-voltage=230V` | `["processInterface","control-data","230V","production-data"]` |
| 2 | Leave blank | `feature-operating-voltage=400V` | `["processInterface","control-data","400V","production-data"]` |

### Verify

| Data feature active | Voltage | Expected result |
|---|---|---|
| No | Either | Variation point inactive |
| Yes | 230V | control-data, 230V, production-data tags |
| Yes | 400V | control-data, 400V, production-data tags |

Typed conditions are entered as `feature-id=value`; do not add quotes around
the enumeration value.

# 5. Element Property

Element Property assigns an existing model-element or architecture ID to a
reference-valued property.

| Target type | Supported property paths |
|---|---|
| Element | `architectureId` |
| Relationship | `sourceId`, `targetId`, `architectureId` |

For `sourceId` and `targetId`, paste an existing model-element ID. For
`architectureId`, paste an existing architecture ID. The current interface does
not provide a chooser for the realized reference value, so the paste-ready IDs
below are essential.

Create these examples from the full **Variability > Variation Points**
cross-domain graph. Do not use the 150% Preview connector shortcut for these
examples because that shortcut does not currently collect the Element Property
path.

